lop my dark-squared bishop.\n\nReason: I choose **B: f1-c4** because it:\n- Develops a piece actively to a strong diagonal\n- Targets the vulnerable f7 square\n- Maintains flexibility for my knight (can go to g5 later with even more force)\n- Prepares potential castling\n- Creates the foundation for a classical attacking setup\n\nThis is more positionally sound than the immediate N: f3-g5, which Black can defend adequately with proper play.\n\nAnswer: B: f1-c4"}
