akest point (only defended by the king), and attacking it with two pieces creates real winning chances.\n\nReason: Knight to g5 creates a powerful double attack on f7 with my bishop already on c4. This forces Black into a defensive position and gives me strong attacking chances against the uncastled king. This is much more forcing than quiet developing moves and exploits Black's current weaknesses.\n\nAnswer: N: f3-g5"}
